# MUSZKA-MAMUTA — agent rules

You are modifying a fork of `cobanov/fly-connectome-template` (React 18, TypeScript strict, Three.js, Vite, Vitest).
Goal: a browser simulation where a *Drosophila melanogaster* with a MaleCNS v1.0-driven spiking brain eats
creatine powder from a scoop and walks a lab mill for eternity, in the visual style of the viral "fly brain" reels
(dark grid → kitchen table, side HUD, view switcher). Live food is an open KFD tub (photo label wrap, authored Ø/H).

## Non-negotiables

1. NEVER invent neuron body IDs, cell-type names or synapse counts. Every ID used in code must be loaded from the
   MaleCNS v1.0 export in `data/raw/` or from `public/data/brain-atlas/`. If you need a cell type (sugar GRNs, MN9),
   write a data-prep script that looks it up by annotation and emits JSON with provenance. If lookup fails, STOP and
   report — do not guess, do not substitute a plausible-sounding name.
2. MaleCNS bulk files are Apache Arrow Feather. Read with `pd.read_feather` / `pyarrow`. They are NOT CSV.
3. Keep the model boundary explicit: the brain simulation outputs `ActivityFrame` (existing template contract).
   Body animation and the creatine / powder system consume it; they never write into it.
4. Preserve `src/components/Attribution.tsx` and the README credit line ("Built with fly-connectome-template by
   Mert Cobanov"). MaleCNS stays CC BY 4.0, Flybody Apache-2.0. Add a "Methods" panel stating honestly what is
   measured (connectome graph, synapse signs) and what is authored (LIF params, hunger, food chemistry, every
   frame of motion).
5. UI text is Polish with an English toggle. Code, comments, commit messages in English.
6. Performance budget: 60 fps on M1/RTX 3060 at 1080×1920 with ≤ 20k simulated neurons. Heavy loops run in a Web
   Worker or WASM, never on the main thread.
7. Every phase ends with `npm run lint && npm test && npm run build` passing. Add tests for new logic.
8. No backend, no database, no auth, no analytics, no paid SDKs. Static site only.
9. Before large edits, print a short plan and the list of files you will touch. After edits, print a summary and
   manual verification steps.
10. Work in small commits with conventional-commit messages. Never amend or force-push.

## Domain cheat-sheet (VERIFY against MaleCNS annotations before using any name)

- Sweet gustatory receptor neurons (GRNs): Gr64f / Gr5a class, labellar (labial nerve) and tarsal; axons terminate
  in the subesophageal zone (SEZ).
- Second-order sugar interneurons: G2N-1, IN1 (SEZ). Feeding command: Fdg.
- Proboscis motor neurons: MN9 (rostrum protractor = proboscis extension), MN11/MN12 (haustellum), pharyngeal
  pump MNs. Shiu et al., Nature 2024 reproduced sugar GRN → MN9 in a LIF model. This is our ground truth.
- Bitter GRNs (Gr66a) suppress feeding. Amino-acid / yeast sensing: Ir76b class.
- Live food: **creatine powder** (`CREATINE_KFD`, sweet 0.05, aa 0.85) —
  authored, not measured. Drive is still the whole gustatory channel; `sweet`
  only scales hemolymph trehalose yield (low → slow satiety). Vanilla twaróg
  (`TWAROG_MAMUTA_WANILIOWY`) is a test fixture. See
  `src/food/foodProfile.ts` and `docs/METABOLISM.md`.
- Hunger is NOT in the connectome: model it as neuromodulatory gain (AKH raises it, DSK/insulin lower it) applied
  to the whole GRN channel (outgoing weights) and to the MN9 threshold.

  11. MaleCNS has NO sugar/bitter receptor annotations (no Gr64f, Gr5a, Gr66a — zero matches, verified).
    The feeding drive comes from class=="gustatory" AND subclass in {"labellar bristle", "taste peg",
    "pharyngeal sensillum"} (~271 neurons). MN9 is exactly bodyId 10331 and 16949. Never reintroduce
    receptor-gene names anywhere in this project.

    12. Only the feeding gate (proboscis gustatory channel → MN9, MaleCNS) is brain-driven. Flight,
    walking, grooming, sleep and comedy beats are authored motion layered ABOVE the feeding FSM;
    they may read metabolism state but never write into ActivityFrame or the brain worker. Every
    authored behaviour cites its behavioural-literature basis in docs/BODY-MODEL.md.
13. Flybody materials in group `body`: body, black, red (compound eyes), ocelli, bristle-brown,
    lower, brown, membrane (wings). Groups front_left / front_right are separate leg meshes with
    coxa pivots. There is no `wings` material and no mid/hind leg pivots. Use these names.

    Zawsze używaj pełnej składni Three.js dla geometrii. Zakaz mockowania logiki 3D logami console.log. Zawsze podawaj pełne parametry wektorów (x, y, z). Przestrzegaj FSM (Finite State Machine) dla logiki muchy.
    14. 3D geometry claims must be numeric. When changing a mesh position, size, rotation or
    material, state the BEFORE and AFTER numeric value in the reply (e.g. "belt.position.y
    12 → 15.1, roller top 16.2, belt top now 16.2"). A claim without numbers is not a
    completed task. Never report a geometry change you did not compute.
15. No external model files. Props are built from Three.js primitives (Box/Cylinder/Lathe/
    Extrude). Never emit code that loads a .glb/.gltf/.fbx that is not already in the repo.
16. One block at a time. When given a multi-block protocol, implement only the blocks named
    in the current message, run lint/test/build, report the numbers, and stop.